                        <locus from="1" to="3">(fols. 1–3)</locus>
                        <title key="work_10039" type="desc">Account of the funeral of Elizabeth of York, 1503</title>
                        <note>Imperfect (beginning and end missing) and misbound: the correct order is fol. 3, 1, 2. Originally a roll, now bound as fols. 1-3.</note>
                        <incipit defective="true">Item and euery day qwellys hyre noble <damage><gap></gap></damage> of þe Kynges costes and
                           chargyse.
                           Item on Tuesday þe xiiij<hi rend="superscript">t</hi> day of
                           Februarij the Abbot of Barmunessay ded <damage><gap></gap></damage>
                           pontifical<damage>ibus</damage>
                           Item on Wedynysday þe xv<hi rend="superscript">t</hi> day of þe
                           same monethe the Abbot of Saynt Albones dyd þe seruys in pontificali<supplied>bus</supplied>.
                        </incipit>
                        <explicit>Item þe noumber of pouer peopell þat was at the dolle þe same day was xvjti thowsand and v hundreth and euery poulle had iiij d. Item ther was deliuered
                        and geven a torche and a noble to euery parishe chirche of London and the suburbes of the same.</explicit>
                        <note>Pr. Davis pp. 128-30. The final sentence is in a different hand. Other manuscripts: none known. Davis discusses two different accounts, one printed in the Antiquarian Repertory (1775-84) IV.241, and one in College of Arms MS. I.3.</note>
                        <textLang mainLang="en" otherLangs="enm">(Middle) English</textLang>
                     </msItem>
                     
