                        <locus from="4" to="6">(fols. 4–6)</locus>
                        <title key="work_10030" type="desc">Account of the coronation of Richard III, 1483</title><note>(type 1b in Sutton and Hammond's classification)</note>
                        <incipit defective="true"><lb/> ... wyth many  <lb/> ... the Bushope of <lb/>... Rychemond ba... <lb/> estate by her selffe ... 
                           <lb/>comynge the duches of Norfolke wyth other ladyes to ... <lb/> after them commynge knightes </incipit>
                        <explicit>And anon the Kyng and the Quene arose vp and went to there chambers, 
                           and every man &amp; woman departed and went there weys where yt lyked them best, that Jhesu for his mercy geve them good rest. Amen.</explicit>
                        <note>Imperfect: beginning missing. Pr. Davis, pp. 124-6. Originally a roll.</note>
                        <note>Wells Rev. 8:2944 [101]</note>
                        <note>Other manuscripts: Sutton and Hammond divide the accounts of the coronation into five groups (1a, 1b, 2, 3, 4), and list (pp. 263-4) the following other manuscripts of group 1b: College of Arms, MS. I.18, fols. 30r-34v (s. xvi), BL, Harley MS. 2115, fol. 124r-v (s. xvii), College of Arms MS. WY fols. 41v-45r (s. xvii), BL Harley MS. 2035 fol. 245 (s. xvii). </note>
                       
                        <textLang mainLang="en" otherLangs="enm">(Middle) English</textLang>
                     </msItem>
                     
